Patch 6501 (R&C pass 1): build_spu_workloads.py --wws-code-slot IMAGE=LSA.

The generated SPU registry calls spu_wws_set_code_buffer_slot(<image id>, LSA) (patch 6500) for each named WWS policy
module right after registering it, so a title whose policy module keeps the job code buffer elsewhere than 0x1320
(Tools of Destruction: pm_10053d00=0x1330) gets the slot set from the same constructor that registers the module,
before any workload runs. write_registry reads args.wws_code_slots (optional, so existing callers are unchanged) and
refuses names that are not registered images; the LSA must be a non-zero quadword below 0x40000.
Test: tools/test_build_spu_workloads_wws_slot.py (CI runs tools/test_*.py). General; upstream candidate.
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02: only the parse_args context moved (upstream added --handled and
--image-ids, 15265cf8); the slot call already uses write_registry's per-image id (image_ids map or index). Unchanged
otherwise.

